            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FUS01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Henry</forename>
                        <surname>Fuseli</surname>
                        <addName>Johann Heinrich Füssli</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1741-02-06">
                        <placeName>Switzerland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1825-04-16"/>
                    <occupation>artist</occupation>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Henry Fuseli was an eminent painter in London. He exhibited at the Royal Academy and was a friend and competitor of 
  <persName key="REY01">Sir Joshua Reynolds</persName>. <persName key="WOLL01">Mary Wollstonecraft</persName> was infatuated with him at one point and 
  asked whether she could cohabit with him and his wife. </p>
                        <p>Godwin first met Fuseli and his close friend <persName key="BON01">John Bonnycastle</persName> at one of <persName key="JOH01">Joseph Johnson's</persName> 
    dinners on 9 August 1796.  The two embarked on a sometimes strained acquaintanceship, but also a long-lived and consistent one with Fuseli mentioned over 200 times 
    in the diary, mostly occurring 1796-1810, and mostly meeting at Johnson's.</p>
                        <p>Godwin recorded his death.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 5, fol. 60: 7 January 1800</bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
